---
/**
 * The data-reference mechanism, drawn.  This is a diagram of the architecture,
 * not a claim about any particular dataset: it shows what crosses the wire
 * (a short opaque handle) and what does not (the peaks).
 */
---

<div class="card p-5">
  <p class="eyebrow mb-3">How the peaks stay out of the prompt</p>

  <ol class="space-y-3 text-[0.82rem]">
    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="font-mono text-ink-mute">1</span>
      <span class="text-ink-soft">
        <span class="font-mono text-ink">experiment.mzML</span> — 220 peaks, parsed in the server process.
        mzML, MGF and imzML are read locally; vendor formats are refused with conversion guidance.
      </span>
    </li>

    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="font-mono text-ink-mute">2</span>
      <span class="text-ink-soft">
        <span class="font-mono text-ink">load_spectrum(…)</span> returns metadata and a reference.
      </span>
    </li>

    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="font-mono text-ink-mute">3</span>
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <div class="mono-block px-3.5 py-2.5" tabindex="0">
          <div class="text-ink-mute">reference =</div>
          <div class="text-accent-ink">"ptr:spectrum:264a5ae9…"</div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[0.78rem] text-ink-mute">
          An opaque, random, expiring handle — never an address, an id or a path.
        </p>
      </div>
    </li>

    <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="font-mono text-ink-mute">4</span>
      <span class="text-ink-soft">
        Every later tool dereferences it server-side:{" "}
        <span class="font-mono text-[0.78rem] text-ink"
          >validate_precursor · compute_cosine · generate_qc_summary · search_library</span
        >
      </span>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="mt-4 border-t border-line-soft pt-3 text-[0.78rem] text-ink-mute">
    The model carries references, job IDs and verdicts — never spectra.
  </p>
</div>
